<title>POLAND: EXBUD WINS PLN 2.5 MLN CONTRACT.</title>
<headline>EXBUD WINS PLN 2.5 MLN CONTRACT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction company Exbud SA won a 2.5-million-zloty contract to carry out construction work at a hospital in Kielce, southeastern Poland, the firm said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>It said work on the project would last from November 1996 to April 1997.</p>
<p>Exbud also said its subsidiary Exbud-Warszawa SA won a 15-million-zloty contract to build apartment blocks in Warsaw from October 10, 1996 to June 1998.</p>
<p>It also said subsidiary Budmatpol Sp zoo won a 3.9- million-zloty contract to build a swimming pool in Lask, central Poland, from October 1996 to September 1997.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
